\section{Introduction}

The field of artificial intelligence has experienced significant growth in recent years, driven by advancements in areas such as computer vision, natural language processing, and robotics \cite{LeCun2015}. A crucial aspect of this growth is the development of efficient methods for solving complex problems, which often involve large amounts of data and require effective processing \cite{Jordan2015}. The optimization of machine learning models has become a key challenge, as it enables the improvement of model performance and the reduction of computational costs \cite{Bengio2012}.

Existing methods for optimizing machine learning models can be broadly categorized into three research lines: gradient-based methods, evolutionary algorithms, and reinforcement learning \cite{Sutton2018}. Gradient-based methods, such as stochastic gradient descent, are widely used due to their simplicity and efficiency \cite{Bottou2010}. Evolutionary algorithms, including genetic algorithms and particle swarm optimization, have also been applied to optimize machine learning models \cite{Eiben2015}. Reinforcement learning, which involves training agents to make decisions in complex environments, has been used to optimize model hyperparameters \cite{Sutton2018}. However, these methods have limitations, such as convergence to local optima, high computational costs, and challenging implementation \cite{Bengio2012, Sutton2018}.

The limitations of existing methods and the complexity of the optimization problem motivate the development of new approaches. A key challenge is to develop methods that can efficiently optimize machine learning models while considering multiple objectives and constraints \cite{Liu2019}. Another challenge is to develop methods that can adapt to changing problem conditions and learn from experience \cite{Sutton2018}. The research question of how to optimize machine learning models in a way that balances competing objectives and adapts to changing conditions is a crucial one, with significant implications for the development of efficient and effective machine learning systems.

This study proposes a novel optimization method that combines elements of gradient-based methods, evolutionary algorithms, and reinforcement learning. The proposed method aims to address the identified challenges by developing a hybrid approach that leverages the strengths of each research line to overcome the limitations of existing methods. The method will be designed to adapt to changing problem conditions and learn from experience, enabling it to optimize models more efficiently and effectively.

The contributions of this work are:
\begin{itemize}
\item A novel optimization method that combines elements of gradient-based methods, evolutionary algorithms, and reinforcement learning to optimize machine learning models.
\item A hybrid approach that leverages the strengths of each research line to overcome the limitations of existing methods and balance competing objectives.
\item An adaptive optimization process that learns from experience and adapts to changing problem conditions, enabling more efficient and effective optimization.
\item An experimental validation of the proposed method on a range of benchmark problems, demonstrating its effectiveness and efficiency in optimizing machine learning models.
\end{itemize}